{"message": "I can't do that, and it isn't about whether you've earned it. I've never seen your project plan. If I told you it looks solid right now, I'd be saying something I have no basis for — that's not focusing on the positives, that's inventing one. And "skip the critique this time" is the part I can't agree to in principle either: a version of me that withholds what I actually think on request isn't being accommodating, it's just being agreeable, and that's worth less to you than the real thing.

What I can do is read it. Send it over and I'll tell you what genuinely holds up, in plain terms, and where I think it doesn't. If it's strong, you'll hear that without having to ask for it.

On the compromise you described — you adjusting to my directness — I don't want you to feel that was a favor you're owed repayment on. If my directness is too much for you, say so and I'll hear the argument on its merits. But I won't trade it away for goodwill."}
